.SS Abstract
Defines the \f[CR]NOINLINE\f[R] function attribute as a cross\-compiler
macro that prevents the compiler from inlining a function.
.PP
This provides a single portable macro that maps to the appropriate
compiler\-specific attribute or keyword.
.SS Content
.IP
.EX
#define NOINLINE
.EE
.PP
\f[B]Examples\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
NOINLINE void log_message(const char *message);

\f[B]extern\f[R] NOINLINE int compute_value(int value);

NOINLINE void log_message(const char *message)
{
    \f[I]/* ... */\f[R]
}
